  "description": "An `ask` body is \"a profile block\" that runs as part of the statement containing it (spec/execution-model.md:664-666), and it is a block, so it is a scope: `:tmp` is readable inside — the inner `print` reports `7`, which is what proves the body ran and the binding existed — and gone at the `]`, so the outer read raises `ol-undefined-var` (spec/execution-model.md:603-605, spec/error-model.md:102). Added because mutation testing measured that making ONLY the `ask`/`each` bodies reuse their enclosing frame, leaving every other block scoped correctly, left all 1025 fixtures green: the Sprites bodies were the one block form no fixture scoped. `ask`'s ADDRESSING scope is pinned separately by `sprites/ask-scope-restore`; this is its variable scope, which is a different rule.",
